# Check out text files with LF line endings everywhere, whatever `core.autocrlf` says. Builds embed
# some files byte for byte: the keystore migrations are checksummed, so a Windows checkout with CRLF
# would build migrations that no longer match the databases they created. Scripts run through bash
# on Windows break with CRLF too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are stored with CRLF and must stay that way.
*.bat -text
